<div class="figures">
<article class="fig reveal"><span class="yr">1898–1981</span><h3>Leonard Howell</h3><p>Often called "the first Rasta". Preached Selassie's divinity from 1932 and was jailed for sedition. Later founded Pinnacle, the first Rastafari commune.</p></article>
<article class="fig reveal"><span class="yr">Active 1930s</span><h3>Joseph Hibbert</h3><p>Reached the same conclusion independently, having lived in Costa Rica. Linked Rastafari with Ethiopian Orthodox and esoteric traditions.</p></article>
<article class="fig reveal"><span class="yr">Active 1930s</span><h3>Archibald Dunkley</h3><p>A former seaman who studied the Bible for two years before declaring Selassie the returned Messiah. Founded the King of Kings Mission.</p></article>
<article class="fig reveal"><span class="yr">Active 1930s</span><h3>Robert Hinds</h3><p>Howell's deputy, who later led his own mission. Arrested alongside Howell in the movement's earliest prosecutions.</p></article>
</div>
